  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies quantum hidden Markov model (QHMM) kernels for binary symbolic time-series classification, using 500 samples and forward horizon k=5. Reported quantum-kernel accuracies include 0.999/0.980 for predictive SVC with trace metric, 1.000/0.949 for structural SVC with trace metric, and 0.998/0.947 and 0.999/0.977 for the corresponding Bures-metric tasks; the paper also demonstrates IBM Nazca hardware circuits with 5-qubit SWAP-test and 6-qubit projected-kernel implementations, plus a 72-qubit layout for multiprogramming.",
